<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- SpotBugs project decisions: a rule, or a rule in part of the code, that the team has decided not
     to enforce. One Match per decision, with a comment giving the reason, for example:

       <!- - JPA entities share associations by design (reason ...) - ->
       <Match><Package name="~team\.projectpulse\..*"/><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/></Match>

     Unlike the baseline, this file may grow, but every entry is a reviewed decision. -->
<FindBugsFilter>
    <!--
      D1 (off): EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2. Every finding is one of three designs that
      share mutable objects on purpose:
      - JPA entities (144 findings, 23 classes): Hibernate tracks changes through the
        collection the entity holds, and Project Pulse edits entities through their getters;
        defensive copies would silently stop those edits from being saved.
      - Spring beans (29 findings, 26 classes): controllers and services keep the beans
        injected into their constructors; that is dependency injection.
      - DTOs and report holders (46 findings, 17 classes, e.g. UseCaseDto): records and data
        carriers built for one request (by Jackson or a converter), read or serialized, then
        discarded; none computes state from its collections.
      Copying would change entity behavior and protect nothing in the other two groups.
    -->
    <Match>
        <Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/>
    </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
